From: Arjan Filius <iafilius@xs4all.nl>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 10:15:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH v2] drm/nouveau/disp: Prevent divide by zero after screen wake-up

On a Lenovo T430, dock, using DisplayPort and 2 4K external screens, a divide
crash happens in nv50_disp_super_2_2_dp() after waking up the screens when the
monitors were in power save (or switched to another input), because ior->dp.nr
drops to 0.

This causes:
- Screen lockup
- High system load after the issue is triggered
- Hangs during reboot

Fix this by returning early if the link has 0 active lanes (ior->dp.nr == 0)
before doing the division calculations.

Closes: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/drm/nouveau/-/issues/377
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/lkml/69D67A9F-1A56-4814-AE68-50559DED42AF@xs4all.nl/
Signed-off-by: Arjan Filius <iafilius@xs4all.nl>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/engine/disp/nv50.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/engine/disp/nv50.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/engine/disp/nv50.c
index 51c045bdfcbb..ab1bc0898def 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/engine/disp/nv50.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/engine/disp/nv50.c
@@ -1157,6 +1157,10 @@ nv50_disp_super_2_2_dp(struct nvkm_head *head, struct nvkm_ior *ior)
 {
 	struct nvkm_subdev *subdev = &head->disp->engine.subdev;
 
+	/* If the DisplayPort link is inactive (0 lanes), skip configuration */
+	if (ior->dp.nr == 0)
+		return;
+
 	const u32 khz = head->asy.hz / 1000;
 	const u32 linkKBps = ior->dp.bw * 27000;
 	const u32 symbol = 100000;
-- 
